00:10:17,033 --> 00:10:18,368
( groans )

261
00:10:23,206 --> 00:10:24,499
Hi, honey.
Hey.

262
00:10:24,541 --> 00:10:26,834
Look, I brought a friend
home for dinner.

263
00:10:26,876 --> 00:10:28,211
This is Zack from work.

264
00:10:28,253 --> 00:10:29,546
Oh, of course.

265
00:10:29,588 --> 00:10:31,214
It's so nice to see
you again, Zack.

266
00:10:31,256 --> 00:10:32,382
You, too.

267
00:10:32,424 --> 00:10:34,008
You guys haven't
actually met before,

268
00:10:34,050 --> 00:10:35,302
but, boy, are
you both polite.

269
00:10:35,343 --> 00:10:36,719
Why don't you
have a seat, Zack.

270
00:10:36,761 --> 00:10:38,346
I'll get you a beer.

271
00:10:38,388 --> 00:10:39,680
I got it.
Thanks.

272
00:10:42,892 --> 00:10:44,811
So, Zack's
pretty nice, huh?

273
00:10:44,852 --> 00:10:47,021
Yeah, I guess.

274
00:10:47,063 --> 00:10:49,316
So, how would you like
to have a baby

275
00:10:49,357 --> 00:10:51,276
that's half yours
and half his?

276
00:10:55,238 --> 00:10:56,573
Excuse me?

277
00:10:56,615 --> 00:10:57,865
Well, we're talking
about sperm donors

278
00:10:57,907 --> 00:10:58,908
and Zack may be the guy.

279
00:10:58,950 --> 00:10:59,993
I mean, look,

280
00:11:00,034 --> 00:11:01,661
he's intelligent,
he's healthy,

281
00:11:01,702 --> 00:11:02,661
he's athletic...

282
00:11:02,703 --> 00:11:05,206
I mean, he's sperm-tastic.

283
00:11:06,458 --> 00:11:09,002
What...? Chandler,
this is crazy.

284
00:11:09,043 --> 00:11:11,338
What did you
even say to him?

285
00:11:11,379 --> 00:11:12,922
"Come up. Meet my wife.

286
00:11:12,964 --> 00:11:14,549
Give us your sperm."

287
00:11:14,591 --> 00:11:16,301
You know, I invited him
to dinner

288
00:11:16,343 --> 00:11:18,261
so you could get a chance
to get to know him, you know.

289
00:11:18,303 --> 00:11:20,888
I mean, if we go through a sperm
bank, you never meet the guy,

290
00:11:20,930 --> 00:11:21,806
get to check him out.

291
00:11:21,848 --> 00:11:23,099
Chandler...

292
00:11:23,141 --> 00:11:24,601
I'm telling you, he's great.

293
00:11:24,643 --> 00:11:26,436
I mean, even if my sperm
worked fine,

294
00:11:26,478 --> 00:11:28,104
I think he'd be the way to go.

295
00:11:29,439 --> 00:11:31,899
Look, I'm not going
to be a part of this.

296
00:11:31,941 --> 00:11:34,444
You can't just bring
some random guy home

297
00:11:34,486 --> 00:11:36,695
and expect him
to be our sperm donor.

298
00:11:36,737 --> 00:11:37,905
( mockingly ):
O-kay.

299
00:11:39,240 --> 00:11:40,575
Zack.

300
00:11:40,617 --> 00:11:41,618
Thanks.

301
00:11:41,660 --> 00:11:43,077
Do you... do you have a coaster?

302
00:11:43,119 --> 00:11:44,371
I don't want to make a ring.

303
00:11:44,412 --> 00:11:47,248
Tell me about yourself, Zack.

304
00:11:52,045 --> 00:11:53,754
Oh, God, do you
think she heard?

305
00:11:53,796 --> 00:11:55,549
Oh, it'd be so bad
if she heard.

306
00:11:55,590 --> 00:11:57,091
Well maybe she didn't hear.

307
00:11:57,133 --> 00:11:58,552
I'm going to go into
that dressing room,

308
00:11:58,593 --> 00:11:59,636
you stay in here
and I'll talk.

309
00:11:59,678 --> 00:12:00,637
See if you can hear me.

310
00:12:00,679 --> 00:12:01,680
Okay, great.

311
00:12:04,516 --> 00:12:05,892
Oh, thank God,

312
00:12:05,933 --> 00:12:07,519
I can't hear a word
that you're saying.

313
00:12:07,561 --> 00:12:10,647
I didn't
say anything yet.

314
00:12:10,689 --> 00:12:12,691
Well, get back
in there and talk.

315
00:12:13,900 --> 00:12:15,235
I'm Rachel.

316
00:12:15,276 --> 00:12:17,612
It's so annoying when
I put Emma on the phone

317
00:12:17,654 --> 00:12:19,406
to talk with my friends.

318
00:12:19,447 --> 00:12:21,074
What?!

319
00:12:21,115 --> 00:12:24,494
Well, some things are just
hard to say to your face.

320
00:12:25,537 --> 00:12:27,330
Okay, well, I heard that,

321
00:12:27,372 --> 00:12:29,999
which means
that she heard it, too.

322
00:12:30,041 --> 00:12:31,501
We have a problem.

323
00:12:31,543 --> 00:12:33,628
Oh, what are we
going to do?

324
00:12:33,670 --> 00:12:36,172
Just be honest
with her.

325
00:12:36,214 --> 00:12:38,091
Oh, my God.

326
00:12:38,132 --> 00:12:40,594
And it is annoying when parents
put their babies on the phone.

327
00:12:40,635 --> 00:12:41,678
All right, enough out of you!

328
00:12:46,307 --> 00:12:48,893
( phone ringing )

329
00:12:48,935 --> 00:12:50,353
Hello?

330
00:12:50,395 --> 00:12:51,479
( whispering ):
Joey, hey.

331
00:12:51,521 --> 00:12:52,355
I need to talk
to Charlie.

332
00:12:52,397 --> 00:12:53,648
Is she there?

333
00:12:53,690 --> 00:12:55,191
No. She went shopping
with Rachel.

334
00:12:55,233 --> 00:12:56,526
Why? What's up?

335
00:12:56,568 --> 00:12:58,403
Well, I'm meeting
with Professor Sherman

336
00:12:58,445 --> 00:13:00,405
about my being
the keynote speaker...

337
00:13:00,447 --> 00:13:01,489
Oh. How's it going?

338
00:13:01,531 --> 00:13:02,949
It could be better.

339
00:13:04,992 --> 00:13:07,287
He, um, he fell asleep.

340
00:13:07,328 --> 00:13:08,663
What?!

341
00:13:08,705 --> 00:13:10,415
But I already bought my ticket
to Bermuda.

342
00:13:11,708 --> 00:13:12,917
Barbados.

343
00:13:12,959 --> 00:13:14,669
Fine, I'll rent a car and drive.

344
00:13:16,254 --> 00:13:18,005
Look, Ross,
you have to get that job.

345
00:13:18,047 --> 00:13:19,215
What am I
supposed to do?

346
00:13:19,257 --> 00:13:20,634
He's out cold.

347
00:13:20,675 --> 00:13:23,344
In fact, he was
just talking in his sleep before

348
00:13:23,386 --> 00:13:27,890
and evidently, he wants someone
named Fran to spank him harder.

349
00:13:27,932 --> 00:13:30,518
Well, just wake him up.

350
00:13:30,560 --> 00:13:32,103
I can't.

351
00:13:32,145 --> 00:13:34,021
If he realizes that I'm the one
who put him to sleep

352
00:13:34,063 --> 00:13:35,482
I won't get the job.

353
00:13:35,523 --> 00:13:37,442
Ooh, that's a tough one.

354
00:13:37,484 --> 00:13:38,735
Oh, wait a minute.

355
00:13:38,777 --> 00:13:40,612
This happened to me before.

356
00:13:40,654 --> 00:13:42,489
Yeah, I was auditioning
for a play

357
00:13:42,530 --> 00:13:45,074
and the producer fell asleep.

358
00:13:45,116 --> 00:13:48,077
No... wait a minute.

359
00:13:48,119 --> 00:13:50,079
It was me who fell asleep.

360
00:13:50,121 --> 00:13:51,790
Yeah, I mean,

361
00:13:51,830 --> 00:13:55,126
hey, Shakespeare, how 'bout
a chase scene once in a while?

362
00:13:57,796 --> 00:13:59,464
Hey, guys, dinner's ready.

363
00:13:59,506 --> 00:14:01,508
I'm going to go
wash up first.

364
00:14:01,549 --> 00:14:02,550
Thanks.

365
00:14:05,762 --> 00:14:07,054
So, what do you think?

366
00:14:07,096 --> 00:14:08,931
I want this
guy's genes for my kid.

367
00:14:08,973 --> 00:14:10,849
Those eyes, those cheekbones.

368
00:14:10,891 --> 00:14:14,604
Okay, there's enthusiastic
and there's just plain gay.

369
00:14:15,896 --> 00:14:17,398
You don't like him.

370
00:14:17,440 --> 00:14:18,899
I think he's fine,

371
00:14:18,941 --> 00:14:20,985
it's just that we don't know
anything real about him.

372
00:14:21,027 --> 00:14:22,862
I wish we could
get more information.

373
00:14:22,903 --> 00:14:24,823
All right,
just follow my lead.

374
00:14:26,449 --> 00:14:28,284
You guys have such
a great place here.

375
00:14:28,326 --> 00:14:30,411
Oh, thanks, I'm crazy
about our place.

376
00:14:30,453 --> 00:14:32,121
Hey, speaking
of crazy,

377
00:14:32,163 --> 00:14:37,794
do you have a history
of mental illness in the family?

378
00:14:37,836 --> 00:14:39,546
Um, no.

379
00:14:39,587 --> 00:14:42,799
Although I did have an uncle
who voted for Dukakis.

380
00:14:42,841 --> 00:14:46,386
That's really not the kind of
thing we're looking for, Zack.

381
00:14:48,012 --> 00:14:49,514
Okay.

382
00:14:49,556 --> 00:14:53,309
So, um, so tell me,
how'd you guys meet?

383
00:14:53,351 --> 00:14:56,145
Oh, friends first, drunk
in London, you know the story.

384
00:14:56,187 --> 00:14:58,606
I've got a better
question for you.

385
00:14:58,648 --> 00:15:02,318
Do you or any of your blood
relatives have diabetes?

386
00:15:04,487 --> 00:15:06,072
No.

387
00:15:06,113 --> 00:15:09,826
Uh, heart disease,
Alzheimer's, gout?

388
00:15:11,285 --> 00:15:14,831
You guys don't have people
over for dinner a lot, huh?

389
00:15:14,873 --> 00:15:17,667
Oh, we're just
making conversation.

390
00:15:17,709 --> 00:15:19,168
Oh, okay.

391
00:15:19,210 --> 00:15:21,003
Oh, I heard a joke today,
it's pretty funny.

392
00:15:21,045 --> 00:15:23,882
You know what's not funny--
male pattern baldness.

393
00:15:26,551 --> 00:15:28,511
All right,
listen.

394
00:15:28,553 --> 00:15:30,054
You guys have shown

395
00:15:30,096 --> 00:15:31,765
a lot of interest in me tonight
and I'm flattered,

396
00:15:31,806 --> 00:15:33,725
and quite frankly,
a little frightened.

397
00:15:33,767 --> 00:15:35,935
Can we just talk
about something else?

398
00:15:35,976 --> 00:15:37,854
Sure.
All right.

399
00:15:37,896 --> 00:15:39,856
This ravioli's delicious.

400
00:15:39,898 --> 00:15:41,691
I notice you're
enjoying that ravioli

401
00:15:41,733 --> 00:15:43,192
with a beautiful set of teeth.

402
00:15:43,234 --> 00:15:46,320
Did you have braces as a child?

403
00:15:46,362 --> 00:15:47,405
No, I didn't.

404
00:15:47,447 --> 00:15:49,949
Yes!

405
00:15:51,534 --> 00:15:53,912
We're teeth people, Zack.

406
00:15:59,250 --> 00:16:00,877
All right,
let's just do it.

407
00:16:00,919 --> 00:16:03,045
Let's just go over there
and just see if she heard.

408
00:16:03,087 --> 00:16:04,297
Good plan. Okay.

409
00:16:05,548 --> 00:16:08,092
What? Where...
where are you going?

410
00:16:08,134 --> 00:16:09,510
Oh, I'm sorry, Rachel.

411
00:16:09,552 --> 00:16:11,763
I don't have time for your
childish games, okay?

412
00:16:11,805 --> 00:16:14,098
I still have
to go find something

413
00:16:14,140 --> 00:16:17,727
incredible to wear so I can beat
Mike at who's more over who.

414
00:16:23,107 --> 00:16:26,110
Hey, hi, hey,
where have you been?

415
00:16:26,152 --> 00:16:27,570
Oh, trying on clothes.

416
00:16:27,612 --> 00:16:30,573
Oh, re... in the dr...
in the dressing room?

417
00:16:30,615 --> 00:16:32,826
Well, that's so weird.

418
00:16:32,867 --> 00:16:35,244
Phoebe and I were just trying on
clothes in the dressing room.

419
00:16:35,286 --> 00:16:37,997
Gosh, it's such a small world.

420
00:16:38,038 --> 00:16:40,708
Rachel, I heard
you two guys whispering.

421
00:16:40,750 --> 00:16:42,335
Oh, God, you did, you heard.

422
00:16:42,376 --> 00:16:44,086
Okay, let me explain.

423
00:16:44,128 --> 00:16:46,005
No, there's nothing
to explain, I heard you.

424
00:16:46,046 --> 00:16:47,674
Phoebe likes Joey.

425
00:16:51,845 --> 00:16:54,973
Yeah.

426
00:16:55,014 --> 00:16:57,016
I just, I don't understand it.

427
00:16:57,057 --> 00:16:58,893
I mean, Phoebe likes Joey

428
00:16:58,935 --> 00:17:01,729
and then she comes here to buy
a dress to impress another guy?

429
00:17:01,771 --> 00:17:03,857
Yeah, that's Phoebe,
that's Phoebe.

430
00:17:03,898 --> 00:17:06,526
You know,
she just wants them all.

431
00:17:06,567 --> 00:17:09,737
It's like... she's nympho.

432
00:17:11,155 --> 00:17:12,573
Wow.
Yeah.

433
00:17:12,615 --> 00:17:13,825
You know, by the way,

434
00:17:13,867 --> 00:17:16,076
I heard you tell her
not to do anything.

435
00:17:16,118 --> 00:17:17,704
Thanks for sticking up for me.

436
00:17:17,745 --> 00:17:21,165
You are such
a nice person.

437
00:17:21,207 --> 00:17:24,042
I try.

438
00:17:28,381 --> 00:17:30,090
( snoring )

439
00:17:40,267 --> 00:17:42,854
( loud creaking )

440
00:17:56,743 --> 00:17:57,827
Ooh!

441
00:18:01,414 --> 00:18:02,874
Oh, my God.

442
00:18:02,916 --> 00:18:06,460
You really want me to be
the keynote speaker?

443
00:18:06,502 --> 00:18:08,379
Thank you.

444
00:18:11,090 --> 00:18:12,967
You're welcome.

445
00:18:24,812 --> 00:18:26,522
Wow.

446
00:18:26,564 --> 00:18:30,735
You look... stop eating hot.

447
00:18:30,777 --> 00:18:35,656
Which is, like,
the highest level of hotness.

448
00:18:35,698 --> 00:18:37,241
Okay. Are you sure?

449
00:18:37,283 --> 00:18:39,786
'Cause I am really dreading
going to this party.

450
00:18:39,827 --> 00:18:40,954
Then don't go.

451
00:18:40,995 --> 00:18:42,538
Mike knows I'm coming.

452
00:18:42,580 --> 00:18:44,582
If I don't show up, he'll think
it's 'cause of him.

453
00:18:44,624 --> 00:18:46,292
And then I'm going to lose face.

454
00:18:46,333 --> 00:18:49,837
That's a very serious thing
in my culture.

455
00:18:49,879 --> 00:18:51,631
All right.

456
00:18:51,672 --> 00:18:55,342
Then you go to that party and
you pretend to be over Mike.

457
00:18:55,384 --> 00:18:57,303
And afterward,
you come to my place

458
00:18:57,344 --> 00:18:59,179
and I'll get you good and drunk.

459
00:18:59,221 --> 00:19:00,974
You got it. Okay.

460
00:19:01,015 --> 00:19:03,768
But not on the wine
that you made, okay?

461
00:19:03,810 --> 00:19:06,854
'Cause I just don't want to go
want to the emergency room.

462
00:19:06,896 --> 00:19:08,314
Okay.

463
00:19:16,823 --> 00:19:19,033
David?

464
00:19:19,075 --> 00:19:21,368
Phoebe. Hi.

465
00:19:21,410 --> 00:19:23,245
Oh, my God.

466
00:19:23,287 --> 00:19:24,580
Wow.

467
00:19:24,622 --> 00:19:26,332
You look unbelievable.

468
00:19:26,373 --> 00:19:28,292
Oh, yeah, well...

469
00:19:28,334 --> 00:19:31,921
Wha... what are you doing here?

470
00:19:31,963 --> 00:19:34,966
Well, I'm back from Minsk.
Permanently.

471
00:19:35,008 --> 00:19:37,051
What happened?

472
00:19:37,093 --> 00:19:38,803
Well, remember how I was
trying to achieve

473
00:19:38,845 --> 00:19:40,930
the positronic distillation
of subatomic particles?

474
00:19:40,972 --> 00:19:43,641
Yeah.

475
00:19:43,683 --> 00:19:46,560
Well, after eight years
of research,

476
00:19:46,602 --> 00:19:49,647
I discovered that...
it can't be done.

477
00:19:49,689 --> 00:19:53,484
Well, it's great
that you're back.

478
00:19:53,526 --> 00:19:54,819
How are you?

479
00:19:54,861 --> 00:19:56,195
Good, good.
Life is good.

480
00:19:56,236 --> 00:19:57,530
Good.

481
00:19:57,571 --> 00:19:59,448
Um, well, I'm...
I'm seeing someone.

482
00:19:59,490 --> 00:20:02,035
Oh, good for you.

483
00:20:02,076 --> 00:20:04,244
Yeah. She's also
a scientist.

484
00:20:04,286 --> 00:20:07,165
So she's very smart
and pretty, and...

485
00:20:07,206 --> 00:20:09,667
Well, it's actually
because of you, really,

486
00:20:09,709 --> 00:20:11,044
that we're together.

487
00:20:11,085 --> 00:20:13,087
I saw what you had
with that Mike guy,

488
00:20:13,129 --> 00:20:15,089
and I just said,
boy, I want that.

489
00:20:15,131 --> 00:20:17,091
Mike and I broke up.

490
00:20:17,133 --> 00:20:18,176
You're kidding me.

491
00:20:18,216 --> 00:20:20,011
Because I'm not seeing anybody.

492
00:20:20,053 --> 00:20:21,721
I just totally made that up.

493
00:20:21,762 --> 00:20:23,056
Really?

494
00:20:23,097 --> 00:20:24,348
Yeah.

495
00:20:24,390 --> 00:20:26,017
I don't know why.

496
00:20:26,059 --> 00:20:27,894
I'm sorry. I guess I just
didn't want to lose face.

497
00:20:27,935 --> 00:20:29,227
I understand.

498
00:20:29,269 --> 00:20:31,105
Yeah.

499
00:20:31,147 --> 00:20:34,441
Okay, so then, okay...

500
00:20:34,483 --> 00:20:36,903
So we're both living
in New York...

501
00:20:36,944 --> 00:20:38,154
not seeing anyone.

502
00:20:38,196 --> 00:20:39,739
That's so not like us.

503
00:20:39,780 --> 00:20:41,365
I know.

504
00:20:41,407 --> 00:20:43,450
Well... well, this is
probably a stupid question,

505
00:20:43,492 --> 00:20:45,452
seeing that you
look like that,

506
00:20:45,494 --> 00:20:48,664
but, um, do you have
someplace that you
need to be right now?

507
00:20:48,706 --> 00:20:51,751
Well... no.

508
00:20:51,792 --> 00:20:55,213
Do you want to get a drink?

509
00:20:55,254 --> 00:20:56,463
I'd love to.

510
00:20:56,505 --> 00:20:57,715
Great.

511
00:20:57,757 --> 00:21:00,093
Okay.

512
00:21:00,134 --> 00:21:02,720
Do you smell beets?

513
00:21:02,762 --> 00:21:06,015
Oh, all right,
stay upwind of me.

514
00:21:06,057 --> 00:21:09,227
Yeah, okay.

515
00:21:09,268 --> 00:21:10,561
Hey, there's Phoebe.

516
00:21:10,603 --> 00:21:12,772
Is that Mike she's with?

517
00:21:12,813 --> 00:21:15,024
No, that's David.

518
00:21:15,066 --> 00:21:19,028
There's a third guy?

519
00:21:19,070 --> 00:21:21,114
Tip of the iceberg.

520
00:21:21,155 --> 00:21:22,489
Oh...

521
00:21:24,117 --> 00:21:25,910
I'm going to take off now.

522
00:21:25,952 --> 00:21:28,955
You're going to let me
go home, aren't you?

523
00:21:28,996 --> 00:21:31,457
You sure you don't want
to stick around a little longer?

524
00:21:31,498 --> 00:21:32,750
No, no, I should get home.

525
00:21:32,792 --> 00:21:33,751
I'm kind of tired.

526
00:21:33,793 --> 00:21:34,961
Are you just tired now,

527
00:21:35,002 --> 00:21:36,545
or are you always tired?

528
00:21:36,587 --> 00:21:38,965
'Cause that could be a sign
of clinical depression.

529
00:21:39,006 --> 00:21:41,425
No, it's just tiring having
to figure out the age

530
00:21:41,467 --> 00:21:43,136
at which
all my grandparents died.

531
00:21:43,177 --> 00:21:45,429
I'll see you tomorrow.

532
00:21:45,471 --> 00:21:46,847
Okay.

533
00:21:46,889 --> 00:21:48,348
Bye.

534
00:21:49,642 --> 00:21:51,978
I think we found our sperm.

535
00:21:52,019 --> 00:21:54,438
He does seem pretty perfect.

536
00:21:54,480 --> 00:21:55,606
Yeah? You think so?

537
00:21:55,648 --> 00:21:57,024
Well, should I ask him?

538
00:21:59,026 --> 00:22:00,319
No.

539
00:22:00,360 --> 00:22:01,821
Why not?

540
00:22:01,862 --> 00:22:03,948
Just because his
great-grandmother was obese?

541
00:22:03,990 --> 00:22:06,366
Our kid's going to get that
from you anyway.

542
00:22:08,244 --> 00:22:09,578
No, that's not it.

543
00:22:09,620 --> 00:22:12,290
It's just that when
we were asking him

544
00:22:12,331 --> 00:22:14,959
all those questions before,
I just...

545
00:22:15,001 --> 00:22:17,253
I just realized I don't care

546
00:22:17,295 --> 00:22:20,631
if he is the most perfect guy
in the world.

547
00:22:20,673 --> 00:22:21,715
He's not you.

548
00:22:21,757 --> 00:22:24,551
Yeah! He's better!

549
00:22:24,593 --> 00:22:27,138
No, he's not.

550
00:22:27,180 --> 00:22:29,974
And if I can't get
pregnant with you,

551
00:22:30,016 --> 00:22:33,144
then I don't want
to get pregnant by him

552
00:22:33,186 --> 00:22:34,352
or anyone else.

553
00:22:34,394 --> 00:22:36,147
Really?

554
00:22:36,189 --> 00:22:37,648
Are you sure?

555
00:22:37,690 --> 00:22:39,233
Yeah, I'm sure.

556
00:22:39,275 --> 00:22:40,442
Thank God.

557
00:22:40,484 --> 00:22:42,069
Because I don't want
to do this either.

558
00:22:42,111 --> 00:22:43,779
I was just doing it
because I thought

559
00:22:43,821 --> 00:22:45,239
that was what
you wanted to do.

560
00:22:45,281 --> 00:22:50,119
I'm the husband--
I'm supposed to bring the sperm.

561
00:22:50,161 --> 00:22:51,745
That is
so sweet.

562
00:22:51,787 --> 00:22:54,040
I love you.

563
00:22:57,543 --> 00:22:59,670
So, you know,
this leaves us with...

564
00:22:59,712 --> 00:23:02,215
Adoption.

565
00:23:02,256 --> 00:23:04,258
How do you feel about that?

566
00:23:05,718 --> 00:23:08,888
I think I feel okay about it.

567
00:23:08,929 --> 00:23:12,225
Actually I think I feel
really good about it.

568
00:23:12,266 --> 00:23:14,977
Me, too.

569
00:23:15,019 --> 00:23:17,688
I want to find a baby
that needs a home,

570
00:23:17,730 --> 00:23:19,899
and I want to raise it with you.

571
00:23:19,940 --> 00:23:23,236
And I want to mess it up
in our own specific way.

572
00:23:23,277 --> 00:23:26,197
So this... this is it?

573
00:23:26,239 --> 00:23:28,241
We're really going to adopt?

574
00:23:28,282 --> 00:23:30,284
Yeah.

575
00:23:30,326 --> 00:23:32,786
Oh, my God, we're going
to be parents!

576
00:23:32,828 --> 00:23:34,997
We are going to be
great parents.

577
00:23:35,039 --> 00:23:36,332
And it could be soon.

578
00:23:36,374 --> 00:23:37,833
I mean, think about it.

579
00:23:37,875 --> 00:23:39,752
Right now, somewhere
out there,

580
00:23:39,793 --> 00:23:42,963
our baby could be
being conceived.

581
00:23:43,005 --> 00:23:44,965
Wait. If we're lucky

582
00:23:45,007 --> 00:23:47,176
and we're really,
really, really quiet,

583
00:23:47,218 --> 00:23:50,346
we may be able to
hear the sound of
a condom breaking.

584
00:23:56,769 --> 00:23:58,104
Hey, Zack.

585
00:23:58,145 --> 00:24:00,480
Hey, Chandler.

586
00:24:00,522 --> 00:24:02,566
Look, I just wanted to apologize
for last night.

587
00:24:02,608 --> 00:24:04,944
I got the feeling we made you
a little uncomfortable.

588
00:24:04,985 --> 00:24:05,819
No, you didn't.

589
00:24:05,861 --> 00:24:06,486
Really?

590
00:24:06,528 --> 00:24:08,239
No, you did.

591
00:24:08,281 --> 00:24:11,325
Yeah, well, my wife and I have
some boundary issues, you know.

592
00:24:11,367 --> 00:24:13,411
Sometimes we ask
inappropriate questions.

593
00:24:13,451 --> 00:24:14,828
We're working on it.

594
00:24:14,870 --> 00:24:16,289
Here are the boards
for Friday's pitch.

595
00:24:16,330 --> 00:24:17,497
Oh, thank you.

596
00:24:19,583 --> 00:24:21,752
You wouldn't know
if Jeanette's planning

597
00:24:21,794 --> 00:24:23,796
on keeping her baby, would you?

598
00:24:23,837 --> 00:24:28,008
Captioned by
Media Access Group at WGBH
access.wgbh.org

